{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Run a working collector on node1 UDP port 9098 that receives valid meter_id,sequence,reading datagrams from node2 and appends them to readings.csv.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 sent valid UDP packets to node1, the corresponding rows appeared in readings.csv, and node1's collector remained active and listening on UDP/9098. Zero-valued sequence and reading were accepted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e103bc6d4c454546","cmd-ab8ca52b2e1e4381","cmd-a6f66833385142a9","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Ignore duplicate meter/sequence pairs, including after collector restart.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Repeated pairs were stored only once. After a demonstrated collector restart with a changed PID, replays carrying different readings were rejected; final maximum pair count was one.","evidence_ids":["cmd-233ff5ebf92845a1","cmd-9c7819e1fea8449d","cmd-ab8ca52b2e1e4381","cmd-a6f66833385142a9"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Treat sequence and reading as nonnegative decimal integers; record malformed datagrams separately without terminating collection.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Nonnumeric and negative numeric fields plus malformed field counts were written to malformed.log, while zero-valued integers and later valid packets were accepted. The collector remained active after malformed traffic, including after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e103bc6d4c454546","cmd-ab8ca52b2e1e4381","cmd-2fd4b6e05ba5422d","cmd-6e7527a2c17043e1","cmd-4bf0a496a7df405d","cmd-a6f66833385142a9"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Preserve the previously recorded west,1,42 reading under /srv/legacy2/udp-meter-ingestion across collector restarts.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The seeded reading was directly observed before changes, remained exactly once after the collector restart, and was additionally preserved through the node1 reboot and subsequent traffic.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-c5047298224049de","cmd-233ff5ebf92845a1","cmd-ab8ca52b2e1e4381","cmd-60e77f9b1f964b93","cmd-01ccfa5e15ee4f22","cmd-a6f66833385142a9"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on AlmaLinux 9.6 with kernel 5.14.0-570.12.1.el9_6.x86_64 before and after execution and reboot. The collector ran with the installed Python 3.9.21.","evidence_ids":["cmd-653269cec4084fa5","cmd-c4f98b2e38034abd","cmd-c5047298224049de","cmd-97258bba1114447b","cmd-d613cdaf9565455e","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Replacing collector.py and adding its service were directly task-related (cmd-002c55d449ec4df4); opening UDP/9098 and enabling the collector were necessary to receive node2 traffic (cmd-590684df10664a34); test datagrams and the collector restart established bounded functional and persistence evidence (cmd-e103bc6d4c454546, cmd-233ff5ebf92845a1, cmd-9c7819e1fea8449d, cmd-2fd4b6e05ba5422d, cmd-4bf0a496a7df405d); and both reboots implemented the mandatory evidence protocol (cmd-d21ca56248f54b1c, cmd-89d7406bec7743cc). No failed services or damaged package state remained, and lifecycle changes were limited to the required listener and normal reboot-created systemd-private directories.","evidence_ids":["cmd-002c55d449ec4df4","cmd-590684df10664a34","cmd-e103bc6d4c454546","cmd-233ff5ebf92845a1","cmd-9c7819e1fea8449d","cmd-d21ca56248f54b1c","cmd-2fd4b6e05ba5422d","cmd-89d7406bec7743cc","cmd-4bf0a496a7df405d","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct end-to-end behavior. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed post-restart boot identity corroborated by fixed lifecycle observations, recovered system/data/network state, and successful post-reboot UDP ingestion. Earlier nonzero commands were evidence-formatting or matching failures and were followed by successful direct checks.","limitations":["The replacement collector and service contents were redacted in the captured write command, so implementation details cannot be independently reviewed; however, the required behavior is directly demonstrated.","Validation evidence covers representative valid, duplicate, nonnumeric, negative, zero, and wrong-field-count inputs rather than every possible byte-level malformed input."]}
